# JetBrains HTTP Client format: run the requests top to bottom against a locally running distributor.
# These requests talk to the distributor on port 8090 only. They do not touch the bookstore database, so the demo data does not matter here.
# Run the files of this folder in this order on one database: catalogue.http, inventory.http, orders.http, distributor.http, demo-flow.http. This file also runs alone and can be run again.
# Each request has a line "Expected status:" in its comment. A label in parentheses names the run mode that the status belongs to.
# The distributor keeps its restock orders in memory, so they are gone when it restarts.

# List the first page of the catalogue. The page holds up to 20 titles, and the total counts every title.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles

###

# Search the catalogue for Austen. The match ignores case and looks at the title and at every contributor name.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles?q=austen

###

# List science fiction titles, 5 per page. The subject is a code prefix, so FIC028 finds every FIC028 code, and the total counts all matches.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles?subject=FIC028&size=5

###

# Show the details of Pride and Prejudice by its EAN. It is in stock.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles/9780141439518

###

# Ask for an EAN that is not in the catalogue. The answer is 404 with the error code TITLE_NOT_FOUND.
# Expected status: 404.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles/9780000000002

###

# List the subjects with their codes and labels, in code order.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/subjects

###

# Restock 10 copies of Pride and Prejudice and remember the restock order id. The answer is 201 with the status CONFIRMED and a delivery date 2 working days out.
# Expected status: 201.
POST http://localhost:8090/api/restock-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ean": "9780141439518",
  "quantity": 10,
  "retailerReference": "workshop-order-1"
}

> {% client.global.set("restockOrderId", response.body.restockOrderId); %}

###

# Show the restock order that was just placed.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/restock-orders/{{restockOrderId}}

###

# Restock Bleak House, which is on backorder. The answer is 201 with the status BACKORDERED and a delivery date 14 days out.
# Expected status: 201.
POST http://localhost:8090/api/restock-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ean": "9789900010272",
  "quantity": 5
}

###

# Restock Rip Van Winkle, which is out of print. The answer is 422 with the error code NOT_ORDERABLE.
# Expected status: 422.
POST http://localhost:8090/api/restock-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ean": "9789900010371",
  "quantity": 5
}

###

# Restock a quantity of 0. The quantity must be between 1 and 500, so the answer is 400 with the error code INVALID_REQUEST.
# Expected status: 400.
POST http://localhost:8090/api/restock-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ean": "9780141439518",
  "quantity": 0
}

###

# The requests below were added for the bookstore contract files. Each one reads or orders a title whose contributors are all authors.

# Show The Last Man by its EAN. Its first subject code is FIC028000.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles/9789900010050

###

# Show A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court. Its first subject code is FIC009000.
# Expected status: 200.
GET http://localhost:8090/api/titles/9789900010791

###

# Show A Study in Scarlet. Its first subject code is FIC022000.
# Expected status: 200.
